text:
sara: quick q — trying to conditionally pull a service token from an ExternalSecret in our helm chart and fall back to a static value per-cluster. when I run `helm template` it sometimes panics with 'nil pointer evaluating interface {} .data' on some clusters. snippet I'm experimenting with:

```yaml
{{- $s := lookup "v1" "Secret" .Release.Namespace "redwood-service-token" }}
service_token: {{ $s.data.token | b64dec | quote }}
```

How do I guard properly so the template doesn't blow up? Is `lookup` allowed during `helm template`/dry-run? Should I use `with`/`index` or check for `not $s`? Any pattern we already use in other charts?

amir: lookup is allowed but it can return nil. do something like this:

```yaml
{{- $s := lookup "v1" "Secret" .Release.Namespace "redwood-service-token" }}
{{- if $s }}
service_token: {{ index $s.data "token" | b64dec | quote }}
{{- else }}
service_token: {{ .Values.service.token | quote }}
{{- end }}
```

`index` avoids dot-traversal on a nil object. alternatively `with $s` ... `end` also guards. note: for `helm template` (client-side rendering) lookup might not be able to query a remote cluster in some setups; `helm install --dry-run --debug` against a live cluster is the only way to exercise lookup fully.

maria: +1. also remember ExternalSecret controllers create the Secret asynchronously, so on a fresh cluster the Secret won't exist on first install. either accept an empty value and let the controller reconcile, or add post-install steps / `--wait`. I usually add a README note that the secret is optional and show how to `--set service.token=...` for CI.

cj: can we add a small helper in chart-helpers that standardizes this pattern? e.g. a template like `{{- include "chart.helpers.secretToken" . }}` that returns token or fallback. pinging @platform for thoughts.

infra-bot: reminder: if your release depends on a pre-existing Secret, mark it in the docs and consider `helm --wait` or a pre-install hook. filed INF-834 to add a recommended helper template in the internal chart-library.

sara: perfect, thanks everyone. i'll switch to the `index` + `if` guard, add the README note about ExternalSecret timing, and open a PR that references INF-834. will ping once it's up. :thumbsup:
